Practical No.4
Clean and preprocess data by handling missing values, 
duplicates, and outliers using appropriate Pandas functions.

CODE: 
import pandas as pd 
# Create a DataFrame 
data = { 
    "Name": ["Smita", "Akanksha", "Reshma", "Divya"], 
    "Marks": [85, None, 85, 250] 
} 
df = pd.DataFrame(data) 
print("Original Data") 
print(df) 
# 1. Fill Missing Values with Average 
df["Marks"] = df["Marks"].fillna(df["Marks"].mean()) 
# 2. Remove Duplicate Rows 
df = df.drop_duplicates() 
# 3. Remove Outliers (Marks greater than 100) 
df = df[df["Marks"] <= 100] 
print("\nCleaned Data") 
print(df)
